            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The need to improve the population’s health and reduce preventable disease is a major theme in Simon Stevens’ NHS Five Year Forward View. The NHS England chief executive calls for ‘hardhitting national action’ on obesity, smoking and alcohol consumption. Nurses will need new skills to motivate patients to change their lifestyles.</AbstractText>
